WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:05.605
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER): I'm
in the hills outside Wahaka,

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:08.908
and my guides Omar and Pepe
are introducing me to one

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:10.043
of their favorite snacks.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.244
OK.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:12.779
GORDON RAMSAY
(VOICEOVER): I can't

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.748
say I share their enthusiasm.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.623
It's very pasty.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.858
It's very mealy.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.025
It's--

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:26.693
Did it taste
like butter to you?

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.994
Butter?

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:30.897
No it tasted like sawdust,
gone warm, creamed up and--

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:31.865
Pepe.

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:33.833
[speaking spanish]

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.468
[beep]

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:37.871
Wow, they're really good!

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.372
Um, not for me.

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:41.474
I feel kind of bad that
you didn't to like them,

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:44.511
and I'm going to give it a
second try if you're up for it.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:47.447
Something also very very
unique and interesting.

00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:48.782
Let's go.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:53.420
It can't be difficult on
the back of that liquid worm.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:57.157
Everyone will compete
on Gabriela's manner.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.758
Even though they're
not my cup of tea,

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:00.627
I gotta think of a way
of using those worms.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.395
OMAR: For sure it's
going to be sweeter.

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:02.962
Sweeter?

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:03.930
Unique also.

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:05.198
What are we looking for?

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:06.666
We're looking for honey ants.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:07.767
GORDON RAMSAY: Honey ants?

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:08.368
Yes.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:08.868
Here?

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.470
Yeah.

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:12.038
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER): Omar
tells me that these arms come

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:14.841
out at night and collect
nectar from the plants

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:18.411
and trees around them to
produce their own kind of honey.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:20.313
That's the food for
the rest of the colony.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.081
But how do you get
the honey from them?

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:23.483
Oh, you just put
it in your mouth

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.385
and as he's put in your
mouth they're going to pop.

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:26.786
GORDON RAMSAY: Bloody hell.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.321
OMAR: The cool thing is
that the ant doesn't die,

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:30.523
so you just pop it,
drink the honey,

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.759
and then you just put the
ant back into the hole.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:33.460
GORDON RAMSAY: Really?

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:34.194
OMAR: Yeah.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.261
Oh there's some ants.

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:36.396
That's a good sign.

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:36.963
OK.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:37.964
OMAR: Go for it.

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:38.598
Just lay down on the floor.

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:39.532
Gordon.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.634
Oh my god, look
how many we found.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:42.469
[speaking spanish]

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:43.703
GORDON RAMSAY: That's all honey?

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.704
OMAR: Yeah.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:45.939
GORDON RAMSAY: It
looks like a ball.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:46.840
OMAR: Yeah, it's their belly.

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:47.674
GORDON RAMSAY: Really?

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:48.975
OMAR: Yes.

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:50.743
And there are more
hanging down here.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:51.878
[speaking spanish]

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:52.912
GORDON RAMSAY:
There's one there.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:53.947
OMAR: In the hole at the top.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.048
Oh my god they're all there.

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:58.218
There's a hole full of sacks.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:59.219
How beautiful are they?

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.253
OMAR: Wow.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.154
Wow that's plenty.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:02.255
GORDON RAMSAY: 1 2 4 5.

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:03.857
They're all
different sizes too.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:06.059
GORDON RAMSAY:
They're beautiful.

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:07.460
Why aren't they biting?

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:09.295
OMAR: Because they're
Wahakans, their friendly.

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.664
GORDON RAMSAY: The actual
sack is connected to the body.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:14.400
And they're a little
balloons, aren't they?

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.336
OMAR: They look like amber, no?

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.605
So just bite the belly.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.473
You just literally
suck on it's sack?

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.441
OMAR: Yeah.

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.778
[beep]

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:35.855
That's [beep] delicious.

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:37.457
OMAR: Yes.

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:41.461
It tastes like sort of, sweet
honey, strong cider, vinegar.

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:43.863
Before my main course,
this one's my appetizer.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.132
[interposing voices]

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:47.267
OMAR: Oh.

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.434
Just go for it.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.872
GORDON RAMSAY: It's
pretty unique isn't it?

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:53.840
OMAR: Yes.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:01.080
And he' still alive.

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:02.048
It's sweet.

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:03.249
So how come it's so sweet?

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:05.518
Because of what
they collect at night.

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:07.053
All of the flowers
and the nectar

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.555
from the different
plants around them.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:10.156
GORDON RAMSAY: And would you
cook with them, or just--

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:11.891
OMAR: I think it would
be really hard for you

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:12.926
to collect a lot of them.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.360
GORDON RAMSAY: Yeah.

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:17.196
The ants were delicious,
but I can't transport them.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:20.233
Because you suck that
belly off the ant.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:21.968
That's a little treasure.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:23.670
A little nugget of
magic that Wahaka

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:27.273
has as a secret ingredient
that I can't take.

